---@field LoggingConfig? aws.lambda.EventSourceMappingLoggingConfig (Amazon MSK, and self-managed Apache Kafka only) The logging configuration for your event source. For more information, see Event source mapping logging.
---@field ScalingConfig? aws.lambda.ScalingConfig (Amazon SQS only) The scaling configuration for the event source. For more information, see Configuring maximum concurrency for Amazon SQS event sources.
---@field MaximumBatchingWindowInSeconds? aws.lambda.MaximumBatchingWindowInSeconds The maximum amount of time, in seconds, that Lambda spends gathering records before invoking the function. You can configure MaximumBatchingWindowInSeconds to any value from 0 seconds to 300 seconds in increments of seconds.
---@field ParallelizationFactor? aws.lambda.ParallelizationFactor (Kinesis and DynamoDB Streams only) The number of batches to process from each shard concurrently.
---@field StartingPosition? aws.lambda.EventSourcePosition|string The position in a stream from which to start reading. Required for Amazon Kinesis and Amazon DynamoDB Stream event sources. AT_TIMESTAMP is supported only for Amazon Kinesis streams, Amazon DocumentDB, Amazon MSK, and self-managed Apache Kafka.
---@field StartingPositionTimestamp? aws.lambda.Date With StartingPosition set to AT_TIMESTAMP, the time from which to start reading. StartingPositionTimestamp cannot be in the future.
---@field DestinationConfig? aws.lambda.DestinationConfig (Kinesis, DynamoDB Streams, Amazon MSK, and self-managed Apache Kafka) A configuration object that specifies the destination of an event after Lambda processes it.
---@field MaximumRecordAgeInSeconds? aws.lambda.MaximumRecordAgeInSeconds (Kinesis, DynamoDB Streams, Amazon MSK, and self-managed Apache Kafka) Discard records older than the specified age. The default value is infinite (-1).
---@field BisectBatchOnFunctionError? aws.lambda.BisectBatchOnFunctionError (Kinesis, DynamoDB Streams, Amazon MSK, and self-managed Apache Kafka) If the function returns an error, split the batch in two and retry.
---@field MaximumRetryAttempts? aws.lambda.MaximumRetryAttemptsEventSourceMapping (Kinesis, DynamoDB Streams, Amazon MSK, and self-managed Apache Kafka) Discard records after the specified number of retries. The default value is infinite (-1). When set to infinite (-1), failed records are retried until the record expires.
---@field Tags? aws.lambda.Tags A list of tags to apply to the event source mapping.
---@field TumblingWindowInSeconds? aws.lambda.TumblingWindowInSeconds (Kinesis and DynamoDB Streams only) The duration in seconds of a processing window for DynamoDB and Kinesis Streams event sources. A value of 0 seconds indicates no tumbling window.
---@field Topics? aws.lambda.Topics The name of the Kafka topic.
---@field Queues? aws.lambda.Queues (MQ) The name of the Amazon MQ broker destination queue to consume.
---@field SourceAccessConfigurations? aws.lambda.SourceAccessConfigurations An array of authentication protocols or VPC components required to secure your event source.
---@field SelfManagedEventSource? aws.lambda.SelfManagedEventSource The self-managed Apache Kafka cluster to receive records from.
---@field FunctionResponseTypes? aws.lambda.FunctionResponseTypeList (Kinesis, DynamoDB Streams, Amazon MSK, self-managed Apache Kafka, and Amazon SQS) A list of current response type enums applied to the event source mapping.
---@field AmazonManagedKafkaEventSourceConfig? aws.lambda.AmazonManagedKafkaEventSourceConfig Specific configuration settings for an Amazon Managed Streaming for Apache Kafka (Amazon MSK) event source.
---@field SelfManagedKafkaEventSourceConfig? aws.lambda.SelfManagedKafkaEventSourceConfig Specific configuration settings for a self-managed Apache Kafka event source.
---@field DocumentDBEventSourceConfig? aws.lambda.DocumentDBEventSourceConfig Specific configuration settings for a DocumentDB event source.
---@field ProvisionedPollerConfig? aws.lambda.ProvisionedPollerConfig (Amazon SQS, Amazon MSK, and self-managed Apache Kafka only) The provisioned mode configuration for the event source. For more information, see provisioned mode.

---@class aws.lambda.CreateFunctionRequest
---@field FunctionName aws.lambda.FunctionName The name or ARN of the Lambda function.
---@field Runtime? aws.lambda.Runtime|string The identifier of the function's runtime. Runtime is required if the deployment package is a .zip file archive. Specifying a runtime results in an error if you're deploying a function using a container image.
---@field Role aws.lambda.RoleArn The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the function's execution role.
---@field Handler? aws.lambda.Handler The name of the method within your code that Lambda calls to run your function. Handler is required if the deployment package is a .zip file archive. The format includes the file name. It can also include namespaces and other qualifiers, depending on the runtime. For more information, see Lambda programming model.
---@field Code aws.lambda.FunctionCode The code for the function.
---@field Description? aws.lambda.Description A description of the function.
---@field Timeout? aws.lambda.Timeout The amount of time (in seconds) that Lambda allows a function to run before stopping it. The default is 3 seconds, and the maximum allowed value is 900 seconds. For functions using Lambda Managed Instances, asynchronous invocations and event source mapping invocations (except Amazon MQ and Amazon DocumentDB) support a maximum allowed value of 5,400 seconds (90 minutes). For more information, see L...
---@field MemorySize? aws.lambda.MemorySize The amount of memory available to the function at runtime. Increasing the function memory also increases its CPU allocation. The default value is 128 MB. The value can be any multiple of 1 MB.
---@field Publish? aws.lambda.Boolean Set to true to publish the first version of the function during creation.
---@field PublishTo? aws.lambda.FunctionVersionLatestPublished|string Specifies where to publish the function version or configuration.
---@field VpcConfig? aws.lambda.VpcConfig For network connectivity to Amazon Web Services resources in a VPC, specify a list of security groups and subnets in the VPC. When you connect a function to a VPC, it can access resources and the internet only through that VPC. For more information, see Configuring a Lambda function to access resources in a VPC.
---@field PackageType? aws.lambda.PackageType|string The type of deployment package. Set to Image for container image and set to Zip for .zip file archive.
---@field DeadLetterConfig? aws.lambda.DeadLetterConfig A dead-letter queue configuration that specifies the queue or topic where Lambda sends asynchronous events when they fail processing. For more information, see Dead-letter queues.
---@field Environment? aws.lambda.Environment Environment variables that are accessible from function code during execution.
---@field KMSKeyArn? aws.lambda.KMSKeyArn The ARN of the Key Management Service (KMS) customer managed key that's used to encrypt the following resources:
---@field TracingConfig? aws.lambda.TracingConfig Set Mode to Active to sample and trace a subset of incoming requests with X-Ray.
---@field Tags? aws.lambda.Tags A list of tags to apply to the function.
---@field Layers? aws.lambda.LayerList A list of function layers to add to the function's execution environment. Specify each layer by its ARN, including the version.
---@field FileSystemConfigs? aws.lambda.FileSystemConfigList Connection settings for an Amazon EFS file system or an Amazon S3 Files file system.
---@field CodeSigningConfigArn? aws.lambda.CodeSigningConfigArn To enable code signing for this function, specify the ARN of a code-signing configuration. A code-signing configuration includes a set of signing profiles, which define the trusted publishers for this function.
---@field ImageConfig? aws.lambda.ImageConfig Container image configuration values that override the values in the container image Dockerfile.
---@field Architectures? aws.lambda.ArchitecturesList The instruction set architecture that the function supports. Enter a string array with one of the valid values (arm64 or x86_64). The default value is x86_64.
---@field EphemeralStorage? aws.lambda.EphemeralStorage The size of the function's /tmp directory in MB. The default value is 512, but can be any whole number between 512 and 10,240 MB. For more information, see Configuring ephemeral storage (console).
---@field SnapStart? aws.lambda.SnapStart The function's SnapStart setting.
---@field LoggingConfig? aws.lambda.LoggingConfig The function's Amazon CloudWatch Logs configuration settings.
---@field TenancyConfig? aws.lambda.TenancyConfig Configuration for multi-tenant applications that use Lambda functions. Defines tenant isolation settings and resource allocations. Required for functions supporting multiple tenants.
---@field CapacityProviderConfig? aws.lambda.CapacityProviderConfig Configuration for the capacity provider that manages compute resources for Lambda functions.
---@field DurableConfig? aws.lambda.DurableConfig Configuration settings for durable functions. Enables creating functions with durability that can remember their state and continue execution even after interruptions.
---@field RuntimeConfig? aws.lambda.FunctionRuntimeConfig The customer-managed runtime configuration for your function. Specifies the customer-managed runtime and the runtime alias that your function uses.

