---A mapping between an Amazon Web Services resource and a Lambda function. For details, see CreateEventSourceMapping.
---@class aws.lambda.EventSourceMappingConfiguration
---@field UUID? aws.lambda.UUIDString The identifier of the event source mapping.
---@field StartingPosition? aws.lambda.EventSourcePosition The position in a stream from which to start reading. Required for Amazon Kinesis and Amazon DynamoDB Stream event sources. AT_TIMESTAMP is supported only for Amazon Kinesis streams, Amazon DocumentDB, Amazon MSK, and self-managed Apache Kafka.
---@field StartingPositionTimestamp? aws.lambda.Date With StartingPosition set to AT_TIMESTAMP, the time from which to start reading. StartingPositionTimestamp cannot be in the future.
---@field BatchSize? aws.lambda.BatchSize The maximum number of records in each batch that Lambda pulls from your stream or queue and sends to your function. Lambda passes all of the records in the batch to the function in a single call, up to the payload limit for synchronous invocation (6 MB).
---@field MaximumBatchingWindowInSeconds? aws.lambda.MaximumBatchingWindowInSeconds The maximum amount of time, in seconds, that Lambda spends gathering records before invoking the function. You can configure MaximumBatchingWindowInSeconds to any value from 0 seconds to 300 seconds in increments of seconds.
---@field ParallelizationFactor? aws.lambda.ParallelizationFactor (Kinesis and DynamoDB Streams only) The number of batches to process concurrently from each shard. The default value is 1.
---@field EventSourceArn? aws.lambda.Arn The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the event source.
---@field FilterCriteria? aws.lambda.FilterCriteria An object that defines the filter criteria that determine whether Lambda should process an event. For more information, see Lambda event filtering.
---@field FilterCriteriaError? aws.lambda.FilterCriteriaError An object that contains details about an error related to filter criteria encryption.
---@field KMSKeyArn? aws.lambda.KMSKeyArn The ARN of the Key Management Service (KMS) customer managed key that Lambda uses to encrypt your function's filter criteria.
---@field MetricsConfig? aws.lambda.EventSourceMappingMetricsConfig The metrics configuration for your event source. For more information, see Event source mapping metrics.
---@field LoggingConfig? aws.lambda.EventSourceMappingLoggingConfig (Amazon MSK, and self-managed Apache Kafka only) The logging configuration for your event source. For more information, see Event source mapping logging.
---@field ScalingConfig? aws.lambda.ScalingConfig (Amazon SQS only) The scaling configuration for the event source. For more information, see Configuring maximum concurrency for Amazon SQS event sources.
---@field FunctionArn? aws.lambda.FunctionArn The ARN of the Lambda function.
---@field LastModified? aws.lambda.Date The date that the event source mapping was last updated or that its state changed.
---@field LastProcessingResult? aws.lambda.String The result of the event source mapping's last processing attempt.
---@field State? aws.lambda.String The state of the event source mapping. It can be one of the following: Creating, Enabling, Enabled, Disabling, Disabled, Updating, or Deleting.
---@field StateTransitionReason? aws.lambda.String Indicates whether a user or Lambda made the last change to the event source mapping.
---@field DestinationConfig? aws.lambda.DestinationConfig (Kinesis, DynamoDB Streams, Amazon MSK, and self-managed Apache Kafka) A configuration object that specifies the destination of an event after Lambda processes it.
---@field Topics? aws.lambda.Topics The name of the Kafka topic.
---@field Queues? aws.lambda.Queues (Amazon MQ) The name of the Amazon MQ broker destination queue to consume.
---@field SourceAccessConfigurations? aws.lambda.SourceAccessConfigurations An array of the authentication protocol, VPC components, or virtual host to secure and define your event source.
---@field SelfManagedEventSource? aws.lambda.SelfManagedEventSource The self-managed Apache Kafka cluster for your event source.
---@field MaximumRecordAgeInSeconds? aws.lambda.MaximumRecordAgeInSeconds (Kinesis, DynamoDB Streams, Amazon MSK, and self-managed Apache Kafka) Discard records older than the specified age. The default value is -1, which sets the maximum age to infinite. When the value is set to infinite, Lambda never discards old records.
---@field BisectBatchOnFunctionError? aws.lambda.BisectBatchOnFunctionError (Kinesis, DynamoDB Streams, Amazon MSK, and self-managed Apache Kafka) If the function returns an error, split the batch in two and retry. The default value is false.
