---The response from the GetDurableExecution operation, containing detailed information about the durable execution.
---@class aws.lambda.GetDurableExecutionResponse
---@field DurableExecutionArn aws.lambda.DurableExecutionArn The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the durable execution.
---@field DurableExecutionName aws.lambda.DurableExecutionName The name of the durable execution. This is either the name you provided when invoking the function, or a system-generated unique identifier if no name was provided.
---@field FunctionArn aws.lambda.NameSpacedFunctionArn The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the Lambda function that was invoked to start this durable execution.
---@field InputPayload? distilled.Secret The JSON input payload that you provided when you started the durable execution. Asynchronous invocations support up to 1 MB, and synchronous invocations support up to 6 MB.
---@field Result? distilled.Secret The JSON result returned by the durable execution if it completed successfully. This field is only present when the execution status is SUCCEEDED. Asynchronous invocations support up to 1 MB, and synchronous invocations support up to 6 MB.
---@field Error? aws.lambda.ErrorObject Error information if the durable execution failed. This field is only present when the execution status is FAILED, TIMED_OUT, or STOPPED. The combined size of all error fields is limited to 1 MB.
---@field StartTimestamp aws.lambda.ExecutionTimestamp The date and time when the durable execution started, in Unix timestamp format.
---@field Status aws.lambda.ExecutionStatus The current status of the durable execution. Valid values are RUNNING, SUCCEEDED, FAILED, TIMED_OUT, and STOPPED.
---@field EndTimestamp? aws.lambda.ExecutionTimestamp The date and time when the durable execution ended, in Unix timestamp format. This field is only present if the execution has completed (status is SUCCEEDED, FAILED, TIMED_OUT, or STOPPED).
---@field Version? aws.lambda.VersionWithLatestPublished The version of the Lambda function that was invoked for this durable execution. This ensures that all replays during the execution use the same function version.
---@field TraceHeader? aws.lambda.TraceHeader The trace headers associated with the durable execution.
---@field ExecutionDataIncluded? aws.lambda.ExecutionDataIncluded Indicates whether execution data is included in this response. Returns false when IncludeExecutionData is set to false in the request.
---@field DurableConfig? aws.lambda.DurableConfig Configuration settings for the durable execution, including execution timeout, retention period for execution history, and an optional ARN of the Key Management Service (KMS) customer managed key that is used to encrypt your durable execution's payload data, including input, output, and error payloads.

---@class aws.lambda.GetDurableExecutionStateRequest
---@field DurableExecutionArn aws.lambda.DurableExecutionArn The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the durable execution.
---@field CheckpointToken aws.lambda.CheckpointToken A checkpoint token that identifies the current state of the execution. This token is provided by the Lambda runtime and ensures that state retrieval is consistent with the current execution context.
---@field Marker? aws.lambda.String If NextMarker was returned from a previous request, use this value to retrieve the next page of operations. Each pagination token expires after 24 hours.
---@field MaxItems? aws.lambda.ItemCount The maximum number of operations to return per call. You can use Marker to retrieve additional pages of results. The default is 100 and the maximum allowed is 1000. A value of 0 uses the default.

