---@field DestinationConfig? aws.lambda.DestinationConfig (Kinesis, DynamoDB Streams, Amazon MSK, and self-managed Apache Kafka) A configuration object that specifies the destination of an event after Lambda processes it.
---@field MaximumRecordAgeInSeconds? aws.lambda.MaximumRecordAgeInSeconds (Kinesis, DynamoDB Streams, Amazon MSK, and self-managed Apache Kafka) Discard records older than the specified age. The default value is infinite (-1).
---@field BisectBatchOnFunctionError? aws.lambda.BisectBatchOnFunctionError (Kinesis, DynamoDB Streams, Amazon MSK, and self-managed Apache Kafka) If the function returns an error, split the batch in two and retry.
---@field MaximumRetryAttempts? aws.lambda.MaximumRetryAttemptsEventSourceMapping (Kinesis, DynamoDB Streams, Amazon MSK, and self-managed Apache Kafka) Discard records after the specified number of retries. The default value is infinite (-1). When set to infinite (-1), failed records are retried until the record expires.
